---
/**
 * The licensing fact, with its official source.
 *
 * Family rule: say a firm is NEA-licensed only with an NEA source linked, and
 * only once that firm has been checked. No partner has been checked yet, so
 * this states the law and tells the reader how to check. It makes no claim
 * about any particular firm. Source checked on the date in company.json.
 */
import { company } from '../lib/data';
---

<div class="rounded-card border border-line bg-surface p-6">
  <h2 class="text-lg font-semibold">Pest control and NEA licensing</h2>
  <p class="mt-3 text-sm leading-relaxed text-ink-muted">
    In Singapore, companies that do vector control work, which covers pests such as
    mosquitoes, rats and cockroaches, must be registered with the National Environment
    Agency (NEA) as Vector Control Operators. The people doing the work must hold NEA
    licences or certificates. Before work starts, you can ask the firm for its
    registration details and check them against
    <a href={company.nea.vcoUrl} class="text-brand underline underline-offset-2">NEA's list of registered operators</a>.
  </p>
</div>
